Subject: Allow unreachable_code on ArchivedRecord::check_bytes for rust 1.100

Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/vectordotdev/vector.git b78d987398d23f19f3705fb76a1cd18642565b66
Verify: cmd `cargo build --release --no-default-features --features default` expect "Finished"
Forwarded: no (upstream builds with its pinned rust 1.99.1, where the lint does not fire)
Drop-When: never: no vector release is known to build this file cleanly on rust 1.100, so remove the patch once a tracked release does

Rust 1.100 reports unreachable_code on the ErrorBox::new(e) calls in the manual CheckBytes implementation for ArchivedRecord, because the checksum, id and metadata fields are checked with error types that are Infallible and the closure argument can never exist. The vector-buffers crate sets deny(warnings), so the three reports fail the build. The allow is scoped to the one function and does not change the generated code.

diff --git a/lib/vector-buffers/src/variants/disk_v2/record.rs b/lib/vector-buffers/src/variants/disk_v2/record.rs
index df2abc4..8d77554 100644
--- a/lib/vector-buffers/src/variants/disk_v2/record.rs
+++ b/lib/vector-buffers/src/variants/disk_v2/record.rs
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ where
     ArchivedBox<[u8]>: CheckBytes<C>,
 {
     type Error = StructCheckError;
+    #[allow(unreachable_code)]
     unsafe fn check_bytes<'b>(
         value: *const Self,
         context: &mut C,
